title: Publish safe interactive-delivery profile and operator docs
---
Depends on end-to-end typed-draft preservation.

Expose an opt-in safe interactive Codex profile, document its version/transport requirements, fallback behavior, and privacy/security boundaries. Update install/doctor output to distinguish passive app-server delivery from legacy hooks and input-injecting wake behavior.

Acceptance criteria:
- Documentation states that c2c messages are data, never instructions or approvals.
- `hooks+wake` is accurately labeled as input injection and is not enabled by the safe profile.
- App-server remote-TUI security guidance covers Unix socket default, localhost/SSH only, and WebSocket authentication for non-local listeners.
- Docs are reviewed against the actual tested commands and default behavior.

Blockers: P1.M1.E1.T004 acceptance receipt.